This fork is of Drake53's fork (https://github.com/Drake53/CSharp.lua), which makes CSharp.lua compatible with
Warcraft III Lua maps and is published as War3Net.CSharpLua and War3Net.CSharpLua.CoreSystem.

The files below were changed by mdlsvensson in 2026, from Drake53's master (v2.0.4): by a merge of yanghuan/CSharp.lua's
master (C# 11 to 14 support), and by fixes for Moonwell (https://github.com/wc3-dev/moonwell) to collection
expressions, template properties, string escapes, nullable values made text, nullable conditionals, whole-number floats,
project references, the NuGet packages folder, lambdas, returns, primary constructors, object initializers, foreach
loops left early, continue inside a switch, fields named as a base class's private field, a float zero made an
integer in Warcraft III's Lua, numbers written in the culture of the machine, local functions used above their
declaration, returns after a using declaration, nullable structs compared with null, the negation of a negative constant,
patterns in a switch statement's case labels, the core's Deg2Rad and Rad2Deg, which were swapped, a conditional added
to an element or a property, a type's name in a pattern, the order the core disposes several values, a method group in
a conditional, long constant string locals, positional patterns, local functions in switch sections, break and continue
after a using declaration, small integers that wrap, checked arithmetic, private indexers, LINQ that stops early, casts
to ignored classes, switch expression arm patterns, tuples, structs read from collections, string calls, user-defined
++ and --, operator true and false, derived records, with on anonymous types, ref locals of elements, ranges and
indexes, enums as text, exceptions caught by type and catch filters, params collections, chars and enums given as
objects, an overridable property read in its own class, locals shared by switch sections, structs given back through
out arguments, out arguments in a conditional's branch, private static fields past Lua's 200 locals, number formats,
the members of collections, LINQ, StringBuilder, char, string, Math, Convert, BitOperations, HashCode,
StringComparer, BitArray and Span the core lacked, AsSpan from a start, an index or a range, an int's >> of a negative
number, structs set field by field in a nested block or a switch section, the conversions of an initializer's values,
foreach over a span, the integer constant -2^31 and the core's own -2^31, which the game's 32-bit Lua read as a
float, generic method groups, an and/or under a tighter operator, string.Contains with pattern signs, and structs
copied where they are stored or given to a delegate. Each change is in the history of the moonwell-package branch.

